<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marruvium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marruvium was the chief town of the Marsi, on the eastern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fucine-lake">Fucine Lake</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, at modern San Benedetto dei Marsi. After the Social War it became a Roman municipium. Remains of walls, an amphitheatre and tombs survive, and it was later the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of the Marsi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marruvium.jpg" alt="Marruvium" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rudy Massaro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Benedetto_dei_Marsi_portale_Santa_Sabina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
